{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>The smith.</b> When it is in construct state the resh has a pataḥ, and when it stands as an independent noun it always has kamatz gadol. And there is no foreign word in Scripture." "<b>Ma'atzad.</b> An iron tool with which they cut." "<b>And with hammers.</b> A tool with which one makes a hole." "<b>He forms it.</b> From the root צורה, and the correct view is from יצירה." "<b>Also hungry.</b> A description of the smith."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "The bracketed editorial insertion [צ\"ל וכאשר הוא] indicates a suspected omission in the manuscripts; the translation follows the corrected reading."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:56.465088456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}